The FERPA requires almost every university in the U.S. to allow
students to opt out school directories (see refs).

Here at U. of I. the on-line directory, called "ph", allows anyone to
search, but will only return short replies (so it is very, very hard
to dump the whole directory. I believe this was done not to protect
student privacy, but to ensure that telemarketers would have to pay
the university for ability to send us junk mail and calls.

The on-line directory contains only what is in the printed directory
plus some email information plus anyone can get a password for the own
entry and edit it pretty much any way they want any time they want (I
love this feature).

- Carl

